Body rows on the orders table now have 6px of padding above and below the text instead of 12px. The heading row is unchanged. The functional tests pass (16/16), but the visual test for the orders page now fails, as expected.

I added a rule scoped to the orders page in `site/css/pages.css`:

```css
.page-orders .table tbody td {
  padding-top: 6px;
  padding-bottom: 6px;
}
```

I scoped it to the orders page because the pricing page uses the same `.table` class, and its rows are unchanged.

Both the desktop and phone visual tests for orders fail, because the table is now shorter than the approved screenshots. I compared the desktop screenshot with the approved one: the heading row, stat cards and everything above the table are identical. The six rows are tighter, and the pager and footer sit higher. The other ten visual tests pass.

I didn't overwrite the approved screenshots, since they're your baseline. If the new look is right, `npx playwright test tests/visual.spec.ts --update-snapshots` will refresh them.

STATUS: DONE

